  "text": "Oncology - Vet et Nous\nMENU\nSpecialized Services\nEmergency\nBirds and Exotic Pets\nDermatology\nEmergency and Critical Care\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nCardiology\nSpecialized Surgery\nAnesthesia and Analgesia\nMedical Imaging\nPhysical Rehabilitation\nAnimal Behaviour\nAlternative Medicine\nGeneral and Preventive Medicine\nOur teams\nCentre Vétérinaire Laval\nCentre Vétérinaire Montréal\nCentre Vétérinaire Rive-Sud\nLanaudière Region\nMauricie Region\nMontréal Region\nNorth shore of Montreal Region\nQuebec City Region\nSaguenay-Lac-St-Jean Region\nSouth Shore of Montreal Region\nTips\nStarting on the Right Paw\nBoutique\nCareer\nYour Career With Us\nYour Internship\nYour Job Opportunities\nGabrielle Lamarre scholarship program\nVet et Nous Excellence program\nVet et Nous\nAbout us\nCommunity involvement\nShelters\nInsurance\nUseful links\nNews\nBlog\nBlood donation\nShelters\nContact us\nFR\nEN\nMake an appointment\nRenew\nShelters\nFR\nEN\nBROSSARD\n1 866 524-4877\nLAVAL\n1 877 651-2152\nMONTRÉAL\n1 855 671-2746\nSpecialized Services\nSpecialized Services\nOur specialties work in collaboration with your family veterinarian to offer a wider range of specialized care to meet the different needs of your animal.\nLearn more\nEmergency\nBirds and Exotic Pets\nDermatology\nEmergency and Critical Care\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nCardiology\nSpecialized Surgery\nAnesthesia and Analgesia\nMedical Imaging\nPhysical Rehabilitation\nAnimal Behaviour\nAlternative Medicine\nGeneral and Preventive Medicine\nOur teams\nOur teams\nWhether day, evening or night, week or weekend, you always have a Vet et Nous team ready to take care of your companion.\nLearn more\nEmergency and speciality centres\nCentre Vétérinaire Laval\nCentre Vétérinaire Montréal\nCentre Vétérinaire Rive-Sud\nHospitals and clinics\nLanaudière Region\nMauricie Region\nMontréal Region\nNorth shore of Montreal Region\nQuebec City Region\nSaguenay-Lac-St-Jean Region\nSouth Shore of Montreal Region\nTips\nStarting on the Right Paw\nOur support program guides you through your pet’s first year with advice tailored to every stage of their development.\nYOUR NEW COMPANION IS A…\nPuppy\nKitten\nTips\nTake care of your companions for life! Discover a wealth of practical advice for the life of your cats, your dogs, your birds and your rodents.\nEXPLORE OUR TIPS AND CONTENT\nDog\nCat\nExotic\nExotic birds\nVet-Tips Videos\nStarting on the Right Paw\nBoutique\nCareer\nCareer\nThe strength of Vet et Nous lies in our close-knit teams who are dedicated to the health of your pets.\nLearn more\nYour Career With Us\nYour Internship\nYour Job Opportunities\nGabrielle Lamarre scholarship\nVet et Nous Excellence program\nYour Career With Us\nYour Internship\nYour Job Opportunities\nGabrielle Lamarre scholarship program\nVet et Nous Excellence program\nVet et Nous\nVet et Nous\nThe strength of Vet et Nous lies in our close-knit teams who are dedicated to the health of your pets.\nLearn more\nAbout us\nCommunity involvement\nInsurance\nUseful links\nNews\nContact us\nShelters\nBlog\nBlood donation\nShelters\nSpecialized Services\nOncology\nSince cancer affects 25% of the canine population, our specialists are there to offer you all the possible alternatives to ensure the comfort of your pets and thus extend their life.\nAs if he was our own!\nWhy consult in oncology?\nWhen we suspect cancer, the first step is to establish an accurate diagnosis and determine the extent of the disease. Cancer leads to the death of 50% of dogs and cats over 10 years old.\nOur veterinary oncologists are there to guide you through the various possible treatments.\nOur priority:\nensuring a good quality of life for your pet by minimizing the appearance of side effects.\nOur veterinary oncologists\nensure your pet’s comfort\n, and help prolong their life in case of cancer.\nAvailable Services\nIt is possible to determine with the referring veterinarians the best treatment plan for their patients.\nThe strategy adopted depends on a multitude of factors including the type of cancer, its location, the extent of the disease and the condition of each animal.\nWe offer different types of treatment according to your pet’s needs:\nChemotherapy\nTargeted therapy\nImmunotherapy\nOncological surgery\nElectrochemotherapy (available only at Centre Vétérinaire Rive-Sud)\nConsult this link for more information\nChemotherapy\nWe use chemotherapy when a cancer has spread or has a high potential to spread.\nThe chemotherapeutic agents, targeted therapies or immunotherapy are available in several forms. Some drugs must be administered intravenously, others orally or subcutaneously.\nWe can administer a single drug or a combination according to a pre-established protocol.\nThe choice of a drug or a protocol depends on the general condition of the animal, the type of cancer and the financial limits of the client.\nThe duration of a treatment varies according to the drug used and can take from 5 minutes to a day. Prolonged hospitalization is rarely necessary.\nThe side effects associated with chemotherapy are not common, contrary to the protocols used in human medicine. They vary and depend on the drugs used and the individual susceptibilities of the animal.\nUsually, these effects are short-lived and resolve without much intervention. Less than 5% of patients are hospitalized following treatment and less than 1% die from the consequences.\nOur priority is above all to ensure a good quality of life for our patients by minimizing the appearance of major side effects.\nThe animals treated at our centre are entrusted to a technician specializing in oncology who makes sure to provide them with all the special care required by their condition.\nBecause we understand the stress experienced by owners of animals suffering from cancer, all our efforts converge to reassure the owners\n.\nWe are here for your companions!\nDr. Sarah\nBernard\nv.m., IPSAV, DVSc, Dipl. ACVIM (oncology)\nCentre Vétérinaire Laval\nCentre Vétérinaire Rive-Sud\nDr. Louis-Philippe\nde Lorimier\nv.m., Dipl. ACVIM (oncology)\nCentre Vétérinaire Rive-Sud\nDr. Maude\nTouret\nv.m., IPSAV, MSc, Dipl. ACVIM (oncology)\nCentre Vétérinaire Laval\nThis service is available at the following emergency and referral centers:\nCentre Vétérinaire Laval\n4530, A. 440\nLaval, QC  H7T 2P7\n(450) 781-1200\n1 877-651-2152\n(Toll Free)\nCentre Vétérinaire Rive-Sud\n7415 boul. Taschereau\nBrossard, QC  J4Y 1A2\n(450) 656-3660\n1 866-524-4877\n(Toll Free)\nVet et Nous is more than 1200 employees across the province of Quebec who work together to ensure the best care for your companion!\nOur veterinarians\nEmergency\nTips\nBlood donation\nShelters\nAbout us\nContact us\nCareer\nHelp! My dog has\nrun away!\nBlog\nNews\nInsurance\nCommunity involvement\nUseful links\nNewsletter\nReceive useful information and our latest news.\nSubscribe\nCopyright\n2026            Vet et Nous.\nAll Rights Reserved.\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nTerms of use\n|\nPublic Filings",
